   111	
   112	Specific Python requirments can be found [here](./experiments/requirements.txt).
   113	
   114	
   115	## 3. OPTIONAL: Build DyPyBench from Scratch
   116	
   117	### Requirements
   118	    - Python >= 3.8
   119	    - pip >= 22.0
   120	    - python3-virtualenv >= 20.16.6
   121	    - ffmpeg (project requirement)
   122	    - libjpeg8-dev (project requirement)
   123	    - libavcodec-extra (project requirement)
   124	    - Git >= 2.34
   125	    - Docker >= 20.10
   126	
   127	### Steps
   128	1. Clone DyPyBench Repository
   129	    - git clone this repo
   130	2. Build docker image using docker build command
   131	    - docker build -t dypybench .
   132	3. Run the created docker image to start the container
   133	    - docker run -itd --name dypybench dypybench
   134	4. Login to the docker container and execute the bash scripts.
   135	    - docker start -i dypybench
   136	    - ./scripts/install-all-projects.sh > install.log 2>&1
   137	
   138	## 4. Maintainance and Future Support
   139	Due to the substantial size of the image (55GB), uploading a new image for minor changes is impractical. Consequently, we propose implementing a patching mechanism as follows:
   140	
   141	- Patches addressing specific issues will appear in the "Releases" section of this repository; they will be provided as zip files.
   142	    
   143	- Copy the patch zip file into the Docker container and proceed to unzip it
   144	
   145	    ```bash
   146	    # Copy the patch to the docker image
   147	    docker cp patch_XX.zip dypybench:/DyPyBench
   148	    # Inside your docker, in the directory /DyPyBench run this command
   149	    unzip patch_XX.zip
   150	    ```
   151	    
   152	- Execute the command "python3.10 patch_XX.py" within the container, replacing "patch_XX.py" with the accurate script name obtained after unzipping the patch.
   153	    ```bash
   154	    # move to the patch directory
   155	    cd patch_XX
   156	    # execute the patch script
   157	    python3.10 patch_XX.py
   158	    ```
